1
00:00:00,583 --> 00:00:03,250
[dramatic music]

2
00:00:09,667 --> 00:00:12,625
[wood splintering]

3
00:00:12,625 --> 00:00:14,708
[rocks clatter]

4
00:00:14,708 --> 00:00:16,333
[branch snaps]

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,208
[thud]

6
00:00:25,125 --> 00:00:26,417
[Ras sighs]

7
00:00:30,208 --> 00:00:31,250
[thud]

8
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:34,500
[thud]

9
00:00:37,167 --> 00:00:40,167
[emotive music]

10
00:00:40,167 --> 00:00:42,875
[buzzing sound]

11
00:00:46,708 --> 00:00:48,708
My master,

12
00:00:48,708 --> 00:00:50,250
it begins.

13
00:00:51,542 --> 00:00:53,792
Get down to the Shadow Dojo.

14
00:00:53,792 --> 00:00:56,000
Set the Gong
of Shattering in place.

15
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,250
[ominous music]

16
00:00:59,250 --> 00:01:03,417
You! Have the last of the
Theroxian texts been translated?

17
00:01:03,417 --> 00:01:04,875
Yes.

18
00:01:04,875 --> 00:01:08,292
Good. Destroy this place
and everything in it.

19
00:01:10,667 --> 00:01:12,583
What about them?

20
00:01:12,583 --> 00:01:15,417
I said everything.

21
00:01:15,417 --> 00:01:17,417
[all gasp]

22
00:01:17,417 --> 00:01:20,792
We no longer need
the Writers of Destiny.

23
00:01:20,792 --> 00:01:24,458
We are the masters
of our destiny now.

24
00:01:24,458 --> 00:01:25,542
[Cinder chuckles]

25
00:01:25,542 --> 00:01:29,000
[Writers of Destiny whimper]

26
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,375
[ominous music crescendos]

27
00:01:30,375 --> 00:01:32,125
<i>♪ Lost in the unknown ♪</i>

28
00:01:32,125 --> 00:01:33,667
<i>♪ So much to see ♪</i>

29
00:01:33,667 --> 00:01:36,417
<i>♪ Together we will rise ♪</i>

30
00:01:36,417 --> 00:01:39,542
<i>♪ We fight ♪</i>

31
00:01:39,542 --> 00:01:44,125
<i>♪ Be a Ninja for what's right ♪</i>

32
00:01:44,125 --> 00:01:46,167
[logo explodes]

33
00:01:46,167 --> 00:01:48,875
[metal clanging]

34
00:01:48,875 --> 00:01:50,208
[tense music]

35
00:01:50,208 --> 00:01:51,667
You two still with me?

36
00:01:51,667 --> 00:01:53,250
[Sora grunts and yelps]

37
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:55,042
A smoother ride couldn't hurt!

38
00:01:56,458 --> 00:01:59,583
[metal clanking]

39
00:01:59,583 --> 00:02:02,792
[groans] I am not afraid
of anyone or anything,

40
00:02:02,792 --> 00:02:04,250
especially heights!

41
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:05,875
I'm just closing
my eyes to rest them.

42
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:07,292
[metal clangs]

43
00:02:07,292 --> 00:02:09,833
-[rock crumbles]
-[Wyldfyre screams]

44
00:02:10,958 --> 00:02:12,083
[Kai grunts]

45
00:02:12,083 --> 00:02:14,708
[Wyldfyre yelling]

46
00:02:14,708 --> 00:02:16,500
[Wyldfyre grunts]

47
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:18,167
[Wyldfyre pants heavily]

48
00:02:18,167 --> 00:02:20,000
-[Kai] Whoops!
-Whoops?

49
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,542
You're not allowed
to say whoops!

50
00:02:21,542 --> 00:02:23,458
I totally got this!

51
00:02:23,458 --> 00:02:25,708
-[tense music]
-[claw recoils]

52
00:02:25,708 --> 00:02:27,167
Not cool, not cool, not cool!

53
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,083
[Wyldfyre grunts, pants]

54
00:02:32,083 --> 00:02:33,958
-You good, Wyldfyre?
-Yeah.

55
00:02:33,958 --> 00:02:36,542
No thanks to
Mr. "I totally got this."

56
00:02:36,542 --> 00:02:37,958
[metal clangs]

57
00:02:37,958 --> 00:02:39,458
[claw arm whizzing]

58
00:02:39,458 --> 00:02:40,958
[metal thuds]

59
00:02:40,958 --> 00:02:42,333
I totally do got this!

60
00:02:42,333 --> 00:02:44,708
-[rocks crumbling]
-Uh-oh.

61
00:02:44,708 --> 00:02:46,708
-[fireball launches]
-[rock explodes]

62
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:47,958
Huh?

63
00:02:47,958 --> 00:02:49,042
[sighs] Thanks.

64
00:02:50,583 --> 00:02:53,208
[metal clanging]

65
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:56,958
[grunting with joy]
I love you.

66
00:02:56,958 --> 00:02:58,667
I love you, ground!

67
00:02:58,667 --> 00:03:00,458
Come on, it wasn't that bad!

68
00:03:00,458 --> 00:03:02,625
No, it was.

69
00:03:02,625 --> 00:03:04,125
But at least we're
out of danger now.

70
00:03:04,125 --> 00:03:06,417
[branch snaps]

71
00:03:06,417 --> 00:03:07,958
[whirring]

72
00:03:07,958 --> 00:03:09,208
[metal clangs]

73
00:03:09,208 --> 00:03:10,625
Forget I said that.

74
00:03:13,667 --> 00:03:15,625
[Nya panting heavily]

75
00:03:15,625 --> 00:03:17,458
We got so turned
around in that storm,

76
00:03:17,458 --> 00:03:19,417
I have no idea
how far out we are.

77
00:03:19,417 --> 00:03:21,417
I know, but we
gotta get to the ritual

78
00:03:21,417 --> 00:03:24,500
of the Blood Moon before--
[groans]

79
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,583
Not now!
[groans]

80
00:03:26,583 --> 00:03:27,958
No!

81
00:03:27,958 --> 00:03:29,333
More visions?

82
00:03:29,333 --> 00:03:30,792
[groans]
I can't let them come.

83
00:03:30,792 --> 00:03:33,208
Have to force them to go away.

84
00:03:33,208 --> 00:03:34,875
[Lloyd groans]

85
00:03:34,875 --> 00:03:36,958
[dramatic music]

86
00:03:38,375 --> 00:03:40,958
[thunderclap]

87
00:03:40,958 --> 00:03:43,917
[ominous music]

88
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,583
[weapon thuds]

89
00:03:46,583 --> 00:03:49,250
[portal whirring]

90
00:03:50,458 --> 00:03:53,000
[groaning]

91
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,958
[Nya] Lloyd. Lloyd!

92
00:03:55,958 --> 00:03:59,542
-[spell whizzes]
-[Jordana grunts]

93
00:03:59,542 --> 00:04:02,917
Settle down, spell.

94
00:04:02,917 --> 00:04:04,500
I don't know what you
think you've been doing,

95
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:06,917
playing person
with your fake family,

96
00:04:06,917 --> 00:04:09,000
but I know your true purpose.

97
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,208
You're a spell that
can bridge our world

98
00:04:11,208 --> 00:04:12,875
with Nether-Space.

99
00:04:12,875 --> 00:04:15,708
Please, no. I don't wanna be
just a spell again.

100
00:04:15,708 --> 00:04:17,167
[scoffs] Like you have a choice.

101
00:04:17,167 --> 00:04:18,917
You should thank us.

102
00:04:18,917 --> 00:04:21,583
We're helping you to do
what you were created to do.

103
00:04:23,792 --> 00:04:25,750
[door closes, computer dings]

104
00:04:25,750 --> 00:04:27,375
[engine revs, tires squeal]

105
00:04:27,375 --> 00:04:30,042
[eerie music]

106
00:04:30,042 --> 00:04:31,708
[Sorceress]
Ooh, careful, Zane.

107
00:04:31,708 --> 00:04:34,042
Don't wanna fall and
get a bump on your noggin.

108
00:04:34,042 --> 00:04:36,417
-[electricity sizzles]
-[Zane gasps]

109
00:04:36,417 --> 00:04:38,125
I should be able to overload

110
00:04:38,125 --> 00:04:41,125
this Imperium electro-wall now!

111
00:04:41,125 --> 00:04:42,750
[electricity sizzles]

112
00:04:42,750 --> 00:04:44,375
[thuds]

113
00:04:44,375 --> 00:04:46,167
[triumphant music]

114
00:04:46,167 --> 00:04:48,708
[suspenseful music]

115
00:04:48,708 --> 00:04:50,792
[groans]

116
00:04:50,792 --> 00:04:52,083
[yells]

117
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:53,917
[groans]
We've gotta get out!

118
00:04:53,917 --> 00:04:55,958
We gotta get Bonzle
back from that creep.

119
00:04:55,958 --> 00:04:57,417
[fist thuds]

120
00:04:57,417 --> 00:04:58,625
[emotional music]

121
00:04:58,625 --> 00:05:01,750
[surroundings rumbling]

122
00:05:03,542 --> 00:05:06,000
I understand
your emotions, Cole,

123
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,625
but we must remain calm
to find a solution.

124
00:05:08,625 --> 00:05:10,042
He's right!

125
00:05:10,042 --> 00:05:12,167
Any spell storehouse
worth its magic

126
00:05:12,167 --> 00:05:15,750
has a few other trap doors
and secret passages.

127
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:17,000
Great! Let's find them!

128
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,125
Eh, no.

129
00:05:19,125 --> 00:05:20,833
[grunts] Ah!

130
00:05:20,833 --> 00:05:22,167
-[orb magic buzzes]
-Eureka!

131
00:05:22,167 --> 00:05:23,958
[magic buzzing]

132
00:05:23,958 --> 00:05:26,292
[playful music]

133
00:05:26,292 --> 00:05:28,708
-[creature growls]
-Ah!

134
00:05:28,708 --> 00:05:30,542
-[creature growls]
-[metal door clangs]

135
00:05:30,542 --> 00:05:35,500
Okay. Someone turned that escape
hatch into a raging Fang Mouth.

136
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:36,708
Janet.

137
00:05:36,708 --> 00:05:38,125
No big deal.

138
00:05:38,125 --> 00:05:39,208
We'll find another way.

139
00:05:39,208 --> 00:05:41,750
[playful music]

140
00:05:41,750 --> 00:05:46,500
[orb magic buzzes]

141
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:49,667
See? A secret passage.
Come on!

142
00:05:49,667 --> 00:05:51,125
[grunts]

143
00:05:51,125 --> 00:05:52,792
What?

144
00:05:52,792 --> 00:05:55,708
Hmph. The darkness has
been made solid here.

145
00:05:55,708 --> 00:05:58,708
Fine! We'll have to go
through the deadly

146
00:05:58,708 --> 00:06:00,875
and smelly hidden passageway.

147
00:06:00,875 --> 00:06:03,000
It's just behind this door.

148
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,958
It smells like rotten manure

149
00:06:04,958 --> 00:06:06,833
covered in moldy toe jam.

150
00:06:06,833 --> 00:06:08,875
[sniffs]

151
00:06:08,875 --> 00:06:10,542
I-I don't smell anything.

152
00:06:10,542 --> 00:06:13,083
-[door creaks open]
-No!

153
00:06:13,083 --> 00:06:17,583
Don't tell me it's been hit
with an "infinity door" curse.

154
00:06:17,583 --> 00:06:18,750
[door creaks open]

155
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:19,917
[door creaks open]

156
00:06:19,917 --> 00:06:21,000
[door creaks]

157
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:24,083
[funky upbeat music]

158
00:06:26,375 --> 00:06:27,625
[toaster dings]

159
00:06:28,750 --> 00:06:30,542
Uh... groovy!

160
00:06:30,542 --> 00:06:32,833
[funky upbeat music]

161
00:06:32,833 --> 00:06:34,667
[doors clang shut]

162
00:06:34,667 --> 00:06:37,583
Sorceress, there's tons
of magic stored in here.

163
00:06:37,583 --> 00:06:39,500
Couldn't something
"abracadabra" us out?

164
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:42,958
Oh, yes.
Good idea.

165
00:06:42,958 --> 00:06:46,750
Now, if only I could remember
what all this stuff is.

166
00:06:46,750 --> 00:06:49,375
[insects chirping]

167
00:06:49,375 --> 00:06:52,625
Looks like a road.

168
00:06:52,625 --> 00:06:54,708
Any idea which way
we should go, Riyu?

169
00:06:54,708 --> 00:06:57,042
[Riyu growls]

170
00:06:59,792 --> 00:07:01,000
Hmm.

171
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,542
No footprints in this direction.

172
00:07:03,542 --> 00:07:06,833
In the Crossroads, they had
street signs everywhere.

173
00:07:06,833 --> 00:07:08,833
Wish someone made
a sign here that says,

174
00:07:08,833 --> 00:07:12,042
"Evil Blood Moon
Ritual Up Ahead."

175
00:07:12,042 --> 00:07:14,625
Anything to show us how
to get there and stop Ras.

176
00:07:14,625 --> 00:07:15,708
[engine roaring]

177
00:07:21,167 --> 00:07:24,375
[dramatic music]

178
00:07:26,250 --> 00:07:27,375
[engine roars]

179
00:07:27,375 --> 00:07:28,792
Was that the girl from Imperium?

180
00:07:28,792 --> 00:07:30,333
The one who hates Sora?

181
00:07:30,333 --> 00:07:31,833
She's got someone captured!

182
00:07:31,833 --> 00:07:33,667
[Riyu barks and growls]

183
00:07:33,667 --> 00:07:36,458
You're right, she's gotta be
going to the Blood Moon ritual!

184
00:07:36,458 --> 00:07:38,625
But we'll never--
Oop, whoa!

185
00:07:38,625 --> 00:07:40,583
Riyu, you're
a fast little dragon,

186
00:07:40,583 --> 00:07:43,000
but there's no way you can
catch up to a moving vehicle--

187
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,125
[Arin yells]

188
00:07:44,125 --> 00:07:46,000
[Riyu shrieks]

189
00:07:47,708 --> 00:07:48,917
Wow, buddy!

190
00:07:48,917 --> 00:07:50,292
You're really flying!

191
00:07:50,292 --> 00:07:51,875
This is actually happening!

192
00:07:51,875 --> 00:07:53,042
Yes!

193
00:07:53,042 --> 00:07:54,375
Let's go!

194
00:07:54,375 --> 00:07:56,000
[Riyu roars]

195
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,375
[engine roars]

196
00:08:00,375 --> 00:08:04,083
Okay. I sense the tension here,
but we don't have to fight

197
00:08:04,083 --> 00:08:07,292
if we just take the
temperature down a notch.

198
00:08:07,292 --> 00:08:10,667
Taking the temperature
down is never my thing!

199
00:08:10,667 --> 00:08:11,958
[fireball blazing]

200
00:08:11,958 --> 00:08:13,417
[fireball explodes]

201
00:08:13,417 --> 00:08:16,000
[swords swish]

202
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,375
[swords clang]

203
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,417
[metal claws thud]

204
00:08:22,333 --> 00:08:24,583
[metal clanking]

205
00:08:26,417 --> 00:08:27,792
[Kai grunts]

206
00:08:27,792 --> 00:08:30,000
[Kai] Like an itch
I can't scratch!

207
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:34,792
-[fireballs blazing]
-[sword clanging]

208
00:08:34,792 --> 00:08:37,625
[fireball blazes]

209
00:08:37,625 --> 00:08:40,042
Wow! Rontu's training
really worked!

210
00:08:40,042 --> 00:08:41,708
She'd be so proud
of me right now--

211
00:08:41,708 --> 00:08:43,458
-[Sora screams]
-[Sora thuds]

212
00:08:43,458 --> 00:08:44,875
[intense music]

213
00:08:44,875 --> 00:08:46,292
[fireball blazing]

214
00:08:46,292 --> 00:08:47,750
[fireball explodes]

215
00:08:47,750 --> 00:08:48,792
[fireball blazes and explodes]

216
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:52,542
Come on, Wolf wannabes!

217
00:08:52,542 --> 00:08:54,333
I just hung off
the edge of a cliff.

218
00:08:54,333 --> 00:08:56,625
You don't scare me at all!

219
00:08:56,625 --> 00:08:58,833
The cliff didn't scare me
either, by the way.

220
00:08:58,833 --> 00:08:59,875
[metal clanging]

221
00:09:01,083 --> 00:09:02,917
Hey, Kai!
I got your back!

222
00:09:02,917 --> 00:09:04,375
[fireball blazes]

223
00:09:04,375 --> 00:09:05,917
-[metal clangs]
-[electricity sizzles]

224
00:09:05,917 --> 00:09:07,333
[fireball blazes]

225
00:09:07,333 --> 00:09:08,875
-[fireball explodes]
-Ha, "You got my back."

226
00:09:08,875 --> 00:09:10,042
[laughs] Nice pun!

227
00:09:10,042 --> 00:09:11,833
What's a pun?

228
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:17,042
Dang, you've got
moves now, Sora!

229
00:09:17,042 --> 00:09:19,292
Someday you might
be as good as me.

230
00:09:19,292 --> 00:09:21,250
[pants] I'm getting there.

231
00:09:21,250 --> 00:09:23,292
I need more practice.

232
00:09:23,292 --> 00:09:25,583
Please don't tell
Lloyd I said that.

233
00:09:25,583 --> 00:09:26,792
[Kai] Okay.

234
00:09:26,792 --> 00:09:28,583
Now we're out of danger.

235
00:09:28,583 --> 00:09:30,750
[engine roars]

236
00:09:30,750 --> 00:09:32,708
[dramatic music]

237
00:09:36,708 --> 00:09:38,708
Whoever she's got in there,

238
00:09:38,708 --> 00:09:40,292
we have to free them.

239
00:09:42,792 --> 00:09:44,750
[engine roars]

240
00:09:46,083 --> 00:09:47,292
Huh?

241
00:09:47,292 --> 00:09:49,167
I thought it was you!

242
00:09:49,167 --> 00:09:50,500
Sorry I can't
remember your name!

243
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:53,583
Ugh, I hate you Ninjas so much!

244
00:09:53,583 --> 00:09:56,458
[tires squeal]

245
00:09:56,458 --> 00:09:57,583
[Arin grunts]

246
00:09:57,583 --> 00:09:59,042
Get off!

247
00:09:59,042 --> 00:10:01,125
I'd rather get in.

248
00:10:03,792 --> 00:10:05,250
[Arin screams]

249
00:10:07,625 --> 00:10:09,125
[tires squeal]

250
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:12,042
-Whoa!
-[Jordana gasps]

251
00:10:12,042 --> 00:10:13,542
[Arin and Jordana grunt]

252
00:10:13,542 --> 00:10:15,917
What do you think you're doing?
Let go of that!

253
00:10:15,917 --> 00:10:17,292
[Arin grunts]

254
00:10:17,292 --> 00:10:18,500
[dramatic music]

255
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:20,667
[Jordana yells and grunts]

256
00:10:22,458 --> 00:10:24,667
[engine roars]

257
00:10:24,667 --> 00:10:28,083
Ugh! Why can't they
ever remember my name?

258
00:10:28,083 --> 00:10:29,750
[engine roars]

259
00:10:29,750 --> 00:10:31,667
Don't worry!
I'm with the Ninja.

260
00:10:31,667 --> 00:10:33,833
Yeah, your outfit
kinda gave that away.

261
00:10:33,833 --> 00:10:35,583
Why are you in that box?

262
00:10:35,583 --> 00:10:36,833
I just like it!

263
00:10:36,833 --> 00:10:38,208
Very comfortable.

264
00:10:38,208 --> 00:10:39,917
Really?
It doesn't look it.

265
00:10:39,917 --> 00:10:41,583
[Bonzle] What's your
elemental power?

266
00:10:41,583 --> 00:10:43,625
Imperiousness to sarcasm?

267
00:10:43,625 --> 00:10:45,917
-[Arin gasps]
-[dramatic music]

268
00:10:47,625 --> 00:10:49,792
-[buttons beeping]
-[gear shift cranks]

269
00:10:49,792 --> 00:10:51,125
-[accelerator blasts]
-Hang on tight!

270
00:10:52,583 --> 00:10:54,125
[engine roars]

271
00:10:54,125 --> 00:10:55,875
-[Arin moans]
-[Bonzle screams]

272
00:10:55,875 --> 00:10:57,792
-[Riyu squawks]
-[buttons beep]

273
00:10:59,583 --> 00:11:00,875
[metal clangs]

274
00:11:00,875 --> 00:11:02,750
-[tires squeal]
-[engine roars]

275
00:11:02,750 --> 00:11:04,958
[Arin moans]

276
00:11:04,958 --> 00:11:06,208
[brakes squeal]

277
00:11:08,875 --> 00:11:10,000
[Bonzle pants]

278
00:11:11,208 --> 00:11:12,667
First time driving?

279
00:11:12,667 --> 00:11:14,125
Believe it or not, no.

280
00:11:14,125 --> 00:11:15,625
Come on, lemme get you
out of that box.

281
00:11:15,625 --> 00:11:17,708
You can't.
It's magically sealed.

282
00:11:17,708 --> 00:11:19,917
-Maybe my spinjitzu--
-[Bonzle] No time!

283
00:11:19,917 --> 00:11:22,208
Ras needs me for his
Blood Moon ritual.

284
00:11:22,208 --> 00:11:24,000
No me, no ritual.

285
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,083
So we gotta get as far away from
Ras and his people as we can.

286
00:11:27,083 --> 00:11:28,458
On it.

287
00:11:28,458 --> 00:11:29,792
[tires squeal]

288
00:11:31,292 --> 00:11:33,083
[dramatic music]

289
00:11:33,083 --> 00:11:34,583
-[tires squeal]
-[Bonzle grunts]

290
00:11:34,583 --> 00:11:36,375
[Bonzle] You swear
you've driven before?

291
00:11:36,375 --> 00:11:38,500
I used to be a top racer!

292
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:40,917
But not in cars.
In mechs.

293
00:11:40,917 --> 00:11:43,083
And I mostly sat backwards
while my friend drove.

294
00:11:43,083 --> 00:11:45,625
Oh, well that
explains everything.

295
00:11:45,625 --> 00:11:46,750
[grunts and sighs]

296
00:11:46,750 --> 00:11:48,667
[Arin] But don't worry.

297
00:11:48,667 --> 00:11:49,792
We'll be fine.

298
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:51,042
[engine roars]

299
00:11:52,833 --> 00:11:54,333
[contemplative music]

300
00:11:54,333 --> 00:11:55,417
[Wyldfyre] What now?

301
00:11:55,417 --> 00:11:57,458
I want to blast something again.

302
00:11:58,375 --> 00:12:00,375
[footsteps marching in unison]

303
00:12:00,375 --> 00:12:03,458
[ominous music]

304
00:12:03,458 --> 00:12:06,125
More of those clowns heading
toward the Blood Moon.

305
00:12:06,125 --> 00:12:08,250
That's gotta be where
the ritual's happening.

306
00:12:08,250 --> 00:12:11,500
[eerie music]

307
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:15,833
Huh.
That gives me an idea.

308
00:12:15,833 --> 00:12:19,125
Nice. I think
we can pull this off.

309
00:12:21,875 --> 00:12:22,958
What?

310
00:12:22,958 --> 00:12:24,458
Maybe one of them uses a crutch.

311
00:12:24,458 --> 00:12:25,792
[Sora sighs]

312
00:12:25,792 --> 00:12:27,375
Okay, whatever.

313
00:12:27,375 --> 00:12:29,667
I'm sure my leg's gonna
hurt like it always did,

314
00:12:29,667 --> 00:12:32,333
and I shouldn't have had
to rest while you all trained.

315
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:37,375
Huh? It-it
doesn't hurt anymore!

316
00:12:41,375 --> 00:12:43,875
[Wyldfyre grunts and gasps]

317
00:12:43,875 --> 00:12:46,000
What? Are you kidding me?

318
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,708
Rontu was right!

319
00:12:47,708 --> 00:12:49,958
Resting my leg
actually healed it!

320
00:12:49,958 --> 00:12:51,708
Huh! Who knew?

321
00:12:52,375 --> 00:12:55,792
Rontu? I was the first one to
tell you that you should rest.

322
00:12:55,792 --> 00:12:59,542
Yeah, but when a dragon said it,
it turned out to be true.

323
00:13:01,208 --> 00:13:03,250
[Wyldfyre grunts gleefully]

324
00:13:03,250 --> 00:13:05,833
[contemplative music]

325
00:13:05,833 --> 00:13:07,375
[items rustling, box thuds]

326
00:13:07,375 --> 00:13:09,083
[playful music]

327
00:13:09,083 --> 00:13:12,875
An alphabetization spell
probably wouldn't do here.

328
00:13:12,875 --> 00:13:15,542
And morphing into a parrot...

329
00:13:15,542 --> 00:13:17,000
takers?

330
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:20,083
[quirky music]

331
00:13:20,083 --> 00:13:21,750
Eh, okay.

332
00:13:21,750 --> 00:13:23,333
[items rustling and clanking]

333
00:13:23,333 --> 00:13:25,708
Ah, invisible shoes!

334
00:13:25,708 --> 00:13:28,000
-No.
-[shoe thuds]

335
00:13:29,042 --> 00:13:31,250
Hmm, Anti-Gravity!

336
00:13:31,250 --> 00:13:33,750
Oh no.

337
00:13:33,750 --> 00:13:35,708
-[bottle explodes]
-[Cole exclaims]

338
00:13:35,708 --> 00:13:37,750
[playful music]

339
00:13:37,750 --> 00:13:39,542
Anti-Anti Gravity potion?

340
00:13:39,542 --> 00:13:40,792
Pass.

341
00:13:40,792 --> 00:13:41,958
[bottle explodes]

342
00:13:41,958 --> 00:13:43,958
-[Zane yells]
-[Cole screams]

343
00:13:43,958 --> 00:13:46,417
[metal items clanging]

344
00:13:46,417 --> 00:13:49,042
-Ew.
-[Cole grunts]

345
00:13:49,042 --> 00:13:51,042
-[blob squelches]
-[Cole groans]

346
00:13:55,917 --> 00:14:00,583
[playful music]

347
00:14:00,583 --> 00:14:02,625
[Cole] Can anyone hear me?
What happened to my voice?

348
00:14:03,708 --> 00:14:05,042
[blob squelches]

349
00:14:05,042 --> 00:14:07,208
Get this slimy
blob off my mouth!

350
00:14:07,208 --> 00:14:09,583
Hey, it worked!
My voice is back!

351
00:14:11,917 --> 00:14:13,125
[metal and glass clinking]

352
00:14:13,125 --> 00:14:15,167
[Sorceress groans]

353
00:14:15,167 --> 00:14:17,000
-[Sorceress sniffs, coughs]
-[soft ringing sound]

354
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,292
Definitely not that one.

355
00:14:18,292 --> 00:14:20,000
[Zane coughs]

356
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:23,167
[Zane groans]

357
00:14:23,167 --> 00:14:24,250
[Cole gasps]

358
00:14:24,250 --> 00:14:26,458
This is not a desirable outcome.

359
00:14:26,458 --> 00:14:28,208
[Sorceress] Don't worry,
you'll be fine.

360
00:14:28,208 --> 00:14:30,958
-[magic buzzing]
-Huh?

361
00:14:30,958 --> 00:14:33,417
I find this destabilizing.

362
00:14:33,417 --> 00:14:37,833
-[stammering]
-It'll wear off soon... I think.

363
00:14:37,833 --> 00:14:39,000
[potion sloshes]

364
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,375
-But--
-Here, smell this.

365
00:14:40,375 --> 00:14:42,417
Does it smell like
newt tail juice?

366
00:14:42,417 --> 00:14:45,042
What does newt tail
juice smell like?

367
00:14:45,042 --> 00:14:48,250
[sniffs]
Ugh, gross!

368
00:14:48,250 --> 00:14:49,833
-[sneezes]
-[soft ringing sound]

369
00:14:49,833 --> 00:14:51,875
[bottle clanks]

370
00:14:51,875 --> 00:14:54,750
-[whines]
-Eh, should have labeled that.

371
00:14:54,750 --> 00:14:56,542
-[bottles clinking]
-[Cole groans]

372
00:14:56,542 --> 00:14:58,958
Why do you have this?
How is this helpful?

373
00:14:58,958 --> 00:15:01,000
But at least you are adorable.

374
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,083
I'm always adorable.

375
00:15:03,083 --> 00:15:04,208
[Cole sneezes]

376
00:15:04,208 --> 00:15:06,875
[soft ringing sound]

377
00:15:06,875 --> 00:15:08,625
Aha! Found it.

378
00:15:08,625 --> 00:15:11,750
My "Instant Opener" spell!

379
00:15:11,750 --> 00:15:13,958
I use it on stubborn
jars of slugs

380
00:15:13,958 --> 00:15:15,500
with lids that won't budge

381
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:17,792
even after running
them under hot water.

382
00:15:17,792 --> 00:15:19,958
[Sorceress yells]

383
00:15:19,958 --> 00:15:21,667
[bottle smashes]

384
00:15:21,667 --> 00:15:25,333
Hey! I'm sleeping in here.

385
00:15:25,333 --> 00:15:28,542
The good news is you have
lots more of that stuff?

386
00:15:30,958 --> 00:15:33,833
I will admit that
I am out of ideas,

387
00:15:33,833 --> 00:15:35,667
and yet urgency is pressing.

388
00:15:35,667 --> 00:15:36,875
That's it!

389
00:15:39,083 --> 00:15:41,792
[Zane] I cannot see.
Where are we going?

390
00:15:42,875 --> 00:15:44,333
[Cole] The perfect size!

391
00:15:44,333 --> 00:15:45,792
Go through the keyhole
and let us out!

392
00:15:45,792 --> 00:15:48,458
Ah! Now I see your logic.

393
00:15:48,458 --> 00:15:49,542
I'm through!

394
00:15:49,542 --> 00:15:50,917
But the vertical distance

395
00:15:50,917 --> 00:15:52,042
between the keyhole
and the ground

396
00:15:52,042 --> 00:15:53,583
is impossible for me to--

397
00:15:53,583 --> 00:15:54,917
[Zane yells]

398
00:15:54,917 --> 00:15:56,917
-[door creaks open]
-[Cole] Yes!

399
00:15:56,917 --> 00:15:59,292
[triumphant music]

400
00:15:59,292 --> 00:16:01,667
I appear to still
have a problem.

401
00:16:01,667 --> 00:16:02,833
Really?

402
00:16:02,833 --> 00:16:04,708
Should have worn off by now.

403
00:16:04,708 --> 00:16:07,458
Well, I guess you'll just have
to buy larger-sized clothes.

404
00:16:09,708 --> 00:16:12,250
[ominous music]

405
00:16:20,042 --> 00:16:22,042
[Sora] It worked.
We're in!

406
00:16:22,042 --> 00:16:25,792
But there's a lot more
of them than I expected.

407
00:16:25,792 --> 00:16:28,042
[Wyldfyre] And they have
their fancy clanging thing.

408
00:16:28,042 --> 00:16:30,875
[Kai] The Gong of Shattering.
Looks like saving the world's

409
00:16:30,875 --> 00:16:33,042
gonna be even harder
than we thought.

410
00:16:33,042 --> 00:16:34,958
[ominous music crescendos]

411
00:16:37,875 --> 00:16:39,833
[grunts] Look!

412
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,708
[Zane's footsteps rumbling]

413
00:16:44,708 --> 00:16:48,625
[grunts] Flee my impact zone!
[groans]

414
00:16:48,625 --> 00:16:50,458
Told you it would wear off!

415
00:16:50,458 --> 00:16:52,333
[ground rumbles]

416
00:16:52,333 --> 00:16:53,458
[chain clanking]

417
00:16:54,542 --> 00:16:55,708
The Cloud Kingdom!

418
00:16:55,708 --> 00:16:57,833
It appears to be
losing altitude.

419
00:16:57,833 --> 00:17:00,583
That's probably where
they took Bonzle. Let's go!

420
00:17:00,583 --> 00:17:01,750
[dramatic music]

421
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:03,500
[trilling sounds]

422
00:17:05,417 --> 00:17:08,375
Oh, now how am I
supposed to follow them?

423
00:17:08,375 --> 00:17:09,792
I can't--

424
00:17:09,792 --> 00:17:10,792
Hold it.

425
00:17:13,542 --> 00:17:15,000
-[bottle breaks]
-[soft ringing sound]

426
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,375
It's been a while, Hatty.

427
00:17:17,375 --> 00:17:20,625
Let's see if you can
still do your old tricks.

428
00:17:20,625 --> 00:17:23,292
-[magic whizzing]
-[Sorceress exclaims]

429
00:17:23,292 --> 00:17:25,292
See you at the top!

430
00:17:25,292 --> 00:17:26,875
Whee!

431
00:17:26,875 --> 00:17:28,875
[triumphant music]

432
00:17:28,875 --> 00:17:30,167
[magic whizzing]

433
00:17:30,167 --> 00:17:32,458
[footsteps walking]

434
00:17:32,458 --> 00:17:34,458
[suspenseful music crescendos]

435
00:17:34,458 --> 00:17:36,500
[ominous music]

436
00:17:43,375 --> 00:17:45,458
Position the captives.

437
00:17:45,458 --> 00:17:47,083
Move it!

438
00:17:48,125 --> 00:17:52,458
[chuckles] I'm so gonna enjoy
watching you all be sacrificed

439
00:17:52,458 --> 00:17:54,458
to release the Forbidden Five.

440
00:17:54,458 --> 00:17:55,833
[Sora] Sacrifices?

441
00:17:55,833 --> 00:17:57,792
[Kai] Don't love
the sound of that.

442
00:17:57,792 --> 00:17:59,875
They need them to release
the Forbidden Five,

443
00:17:59,875 --> 00:18:01,500
or else the ritual fails?

444
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:03,083
[Wyldfyre] Sounds
like you just said,

445
00:18:03,083 --> 00:18:05,500
"Let's blast their chains
and free them."

446
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:09,083
Wyldfyre, you're always
pickin' up what I'm layin' down.

447
00:18:09,083 --> 00:18:11,958
[footsteps shuffle]

448
00:18:11,958 --> 00:18:14,125
Initiate.

449
00:18:14,125 --> 00:18:18,667
[drumbeat]

450
00:18:18,667 --> 00:18:21,958
[Nokt] Finally,
after long centuries,

451
00:18:21,958 --> 00:18:25,375
we are being called home.

452
00:18:25,375 --> 00:18:27,667
[ominous music crescendos]

453
00:18:27,667 --> 00:18:30,958
Where is Jordana?
She should be here by now.

454
00:18:30,958 --> 00:18:33,958
You ask me, she's super
unreliable, Lord Ras.

455
00:18:33,958 --> 00:18:36,875
You should have sent me after
that spell instead of her.

456
00:18:36,875 --> 00:18:38,875
[Ras growls]

457
00:18:38,875 --> 00:18:40,458
[Sora] Nothing to be afraid of.

458
00:18:40,458 --> 00:18:41,917
We got this.

459
00:18:41,917 --> 00:18:43,500
[Wyldfyre] Who's afraid?
I'm not afraid.

460
00:18:43,500 --> 00:18:45,083
[Sora] I was talking to myself.

461
00:18:45,083 --> 00:18:46,125
Hey!

462
00:18:50,083 --> 00:18:52,083
Lord Ras!

463
00:18:52,083 --> 00:18:55,583
You come here empty-handed?
Where is the spell?

464
00:18:55,583 --> 00:18:58,833
It was stolen by one
of those pesky Ninjas.

465
00:18:58,833 --> 00:19:00,375
You fool!

466
00:19:00,375 --> 00:19:02,208
[thud]

467
00:19:02,208 --> 00:19:03,583
[Ras grunts]

468
00:19:05,917 --> 00:19:09,208
[clicks tongue] Not the
teacher's pet anymore, I guess.

469
00:19:09,208 --> 00:19:12,417
[angry groan]

470
00:19:12,417 --> 00:19:14,167
[Sora] What do you
think all that was?

471
00:19:14,167 --> 00:19:16,792
[Kai] A good distraction.
Let's go!

472
00:19:16,792 --> 00:19:18,083
[dramatic music]

473
00:19:18,083 --> 00:19:19,625
[engine roaring]

474
00:19:22,208 --> 00:19:26,500
[engine roaring]

475
00:19:26,500 --> 00:19:29,042
[Ras grunts and growls]

476
00:19:29,042 --> 00:19:30,500
[engine roars]

477
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:31,750
[Ras grunts]

478
00:19:31,750 --> 00:19:33,083
-[Arin grunts]
-[tires squeal]

479
00:19:37,208 --> 00:19:38,708
[Riyu growls]

480
00:19:38,708 --> 00:19:39,875
[roars]

481
00:19:41,750 --> 00:19:45,458
[Riyu roars]

482
00:19:45,458 --> 00:19:47,125
-[Riyu groans]
-[Arin grunts]

483
00:19:48,750 --> 00:19:50,958
Ninja, go!

484
00:19:50,958 --> 00:19:53,083
[magical whirr]

485
00:19:53,083 --> 00:19:54,208
[Arin grunts]

486
00:19:54,208 --> 00:19:55,458
[dramatic music]

487
00:19:55,458 --> 00:19:58,083
[Arin grunts]

488
00:19:58,083 --> 00:20:00,250
[Arin groans in pain]

489
00:20:00,250 --> 00:20:01,375
[dramatic music]

490
00:20:03,250 --> 00:20:05,292
[Arin grunts]

491
00:20:05,292 --> 00:20:06,667
[Arin groans]

492
00:20:06,667 --> 00:20:08,375
[Arin grunts]

493
00:20:08,375 --> 00:20:10,125
[Arin groans and pants]

494
00:20:10,125 --> 00:20:12,708
[Arin] Ninja never quit--
[yells]

495
00:20:12,708 --> 00:20:15,792
You could be something special.

496
00:20:15,792 --> 00:20:18,292
Too bad the Ninja hold you back.

497
00:20:18,292 --> 00:20:20,292
[groans in pain]
No, they don't!

498
00:20:20,292 --> 00:20:21,875
They're making me better!

499
00:20:21,875 --> 00:20:23,333
[Ras scoffs]

500
00:20:23,333 --> 00:20:25,792
Then how come you
aren't any better?

501
00:20:25,792 --> 00:20:30,042
I stopped you as easily now
as the first time we met.

502
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:34,208
I was weak like you, once.

503
00:20:35,542 --> 00:20:36,750
[buzzing sound]

504
00:20:36,750 --> 00:20:38,667
[Ras] My Master found me

505
00:20:38,667 --> 00:20:42,292
<i>and taught me the most</i>
<i>important thing in this world.</i>

506
00:20:42,292 --> 00:20:43,500
Strength.

507
00:20:44,625 --> 00:20:45,833
[dramatic music]

508
00:20:45,833 --> 00:20:47,292
[Ras grunts]

509
00:20:47,292 --> 00:20:48,542
[Arin crashes and screams]

510
00:20:48,542 --> 00:20:49,708
[rocks rumbling]

511
00:20:49,708 --> 00:20:51,417
[Arin gasps and sighs]

512
00:20:51,417 --> 00:20:53,875
[Ras growls]

513
00:20:53,875 --> 00:20:57,208
Maybe one day you'll
find a true Master

514
00:20:57,208 --> 00:20:59,333
who can teach you the same.

515
00:20:59,333 --> 00:21:02,292
[tense music]

516
00:21:02,292 --> 00:21:05,042
-[tires squeal]
-[Bonzle] Let me go, weirdo!

517
00:21:05,042 --> 00:21:06,250
[engine roars]

518
00:21:06,250 --> 00:21:07,958
[Arin groans in pain]

519
00:21:07,958 --> 00:21:11,167
-[gentle music]
-[footsteps approaching]

520
00:21:11,167 --> 00:21:14,125
Mom? Dad?

521
00:21:14,125 --> 00:21:15,792
[ominous music]

522
00:21:17,125 --> 00:21:19,417
[Bonzle grunts and pants]

523
00:21:19,417 --> 00:21:21,292
[Bonzle] Let me out!
Let me out of here!

524
00:21:22,833 --> 00:21:26,000
[dramatic music]

525
00:21:27,792 --> 00:21:31,333
The pieces are all
in place, Master!

526
00:21:31,333 --> 00:21:34,625
Your patience and planning
are finally paying off!

527
00:21:37,792 --> 00:21:41,333
And the true power
of all the realms

528
00:21:41,333 --> 00:21:43,625
will be ours.

529
00:21:45,042 --> 00:21:47,750
[closing theme music playing]

